{"title":"Dodecagon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">dodecagon</a> is a 12-sided <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygon</a>. The sum of its internal <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angles</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6683281275a193fa111dffd2d14501f2b751af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1800^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. The exterior angles of a regular dodecagon has measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73393067e6d6e401a5354accc7a730c7a2977aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>A regular dodecagon can be seen below:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e12fea08044e8c9b01f003b869951661635201d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for(int i = 0; i &lt;= 11; ++i) { draw(dir(360/12*i)--dir(360/12*(i + 1))); } pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J,K,L; A=dir(360/12*0); B=dir(360/12*1); C=dir(360/12*2); D=dir(360/12*3); E=dir(360/12*4); F=dir(360/12*5); G=dir(360/12*6); H=dir(360/12*7); I=dir(360/12*8); J=dir(360/12*9); K=dir(360/12*10); L=dir(360/12*11); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,dir(0)); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,dir(30)); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,dir(60)); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,dir(90)); label(&quot;E&quot;,E,dir(120)); label(&quot;F&quot;,F,dir(150)); label(&quot;G&quot;,G,dir(180)); label(&quot;H&quot;,H,dir(210)); label(&quot;I&quot;,I,dir(240)); label(&quot;J&quot;,J,dir(270)); label(&quot;K&quot;,K,dir(300)); label(&quot;L&quot;,L,dir(330)); draw(dir(360/12*0)--dir(360/12*6)); dot((dir(360/12*0)+dir(360/12*6))/2); pair O = (dir(360/12*0)+dir(360/12*6))/2; label(&quot;O&quot;,O,S); draw(A--O); draw(Circle(O,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\nThe area of a regular dodecagon can be calculated by the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a30a2f9b5a7ec8e97e08c463500f5e81260b2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3R^2$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumradius of the dodecagon. In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />. Also, each small triangle (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd97737c9a1eb5146725902d4e4c4bda1388129b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d9b534de592b2a7fc63b97e1f0faab799204e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, etc.) is congruent, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45efe2081b6ff9d626e5be38563e82bf7414b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB=\\angle BOC=\\angle COD$\" width=\"216\" height=\"13\" /> (etc) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b4b9350a28cf6b86b6b1ea002e84c5cd4348ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dodecagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">Polygon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Dodecagon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083113\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2622/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.556      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.556      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5154:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018083113 and revision id 285528. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}